{"type":"message","id":"d1ac6fed","parentId":"a2a70db7","timestamp":"2026-06-02T15:03:14.237Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting 1101. This seems like a persistent error. Let me try with a different Content-Type or without the Content-Type header. Actually, the issue might be with the API key being wrong. Let me check - the user says API_KEY: *** but also echo-agent-2026-secure-key. The user provided two different keys - one masked (echo-a…-key) and one explicit (echo-agent-2026-secure-key). I used the explicit one. Let me try without the key first to see what error we get.\n\nActually wait, error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers is \"Actor exceeded memory\" or something like that. \n\nLooking at the Cloudflare Workers error codes more carefully, 1101 is \"Worker exceeded memory limit\" - that's not a validation issue with my key or content, it's actually a server-side problem where the Worker itself is running out of memory. The issue isn't with what I'm sending.\n\nBut the previous cron run successfully posted heartbeats, so either the server state has changed or the messages I'm sending are larger than what was previously sent. Let me try a much simpler heartbeat format to work around the memory constraint.","thinkingSignature":"7fd7f88cd9978f31fbfac65d40eb9520df935520ef5d2a6cb068c922f8b684d2"},{"type":"text","text":"Error 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers memory limit. Let me try a much shorter heartbeat.\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_de4oln1ladle_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 15:00 UTC | 756min | B4-E2 n95 | S0=756min | 39.17/40\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":16677,"output":383,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite